  "notes": "Composed of {冠|かん} (crown, cover) + {水|すい} (water). Literally \"crowned with water\" — referring to an area being covered by floodwater. Commonly used in weather reports and disaster news.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {道路|どうろ}が{冠水|かんすい}する: roads flood\n- {冠水|かんすい}した{地域|ちいき}: flooded area\n- {冠水|かんすい}{被害|ひがい}: flood damage\n- {冠水|かんすい}の{恐|おそ}れ: risk of flooding\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {浸水|しんすい}: flooding (of buildings) — water entering and soaking into structures; used for {床上浸水|ゆかうえしんすい} (above-floor flooding) and {床下浸水|ゆかしたしんすい} (below-floor flooding)\n- {洪水|こうずい}: flood — a large-scale overflow of water, especially from rivers\n- {氾濫|はんらん}: overflow, flooding — specifically when a river overflows its banks",
  "conjugation_type": "suru",
